# `power::Limits`

Reactive, voltage and line limits of the optimal power flow.

## Signature

```cpp
power::Limits
```

## What It Does

The operating limits that `opf` must respect besides the active-power bounds in `GenCost`.

## Fields

| Field | Meaning | Default |
|---|---|---|
| `q_lower` | Reactive-power lower bound of each generator, per unit, `[..., generator]`. | required |
| `q_upper` | Reactive-power upper bound of each generator. | required |
| `vm_lower` | Voltage-magnitude lower bound of each bus, `[..., bus]`. | required |
| `vm_upper` | Voltage-magnitude upper bound of each bus. | required |
| `flow` | Apparent-power rating of each line, applied at both ends, `[..., line]`; leave it undefined to switch the rating off. | undefined (off) |

## Returns

A value; validated by `opf`.

## Errors

A lower bound above its upper bound, or a length that is not the number of generators, buses or lines, is rejected.

## Interpretation and Use

Limits that no operating point can meet do not throw: the optimiser returns the point that violates them least with `converged` false. A binding rating has a nonzero `from_shadow` or `to_shadow` in the result.

